        "origin": "original",
        "lore": "Campaign original (no Muv-Luv canon source). Shenyang's quasi-fifth-generation frame, built to give the PRC a share of the next generation without waiting on Yokohama or Washington. Its power plant, actuators and control system were designed as one, after the fifth-generation definition, but it still flies on fourth-generation jump units and a home-grown control system instead of an XM3 derivative, so it falls short of the true fifth-generation frames. Lighter and cheaper than the J-20, with low-observable shaping and an internal bay for the South China Sea front. The baseline J-35 is navalised for carrier and amphibious-ship operations; the J-35A is the land-based version. Name: Gyrfalcon, after the real-world FC-31 demonstrator. Not to be confused with the Swedish J-35 Draken.",
        "attribution": "original",
        "publishStatus": "published"
      }
